From 391af59ff74dff9bb5348a204dcb46284bd8359c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 21:56:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] mm: convert VMA insert/remove to use per-shard locks

In sharded mode (i_mmap_shards_ptr != NULL), VMA insert and remove
operations use per-shard rw_semaphore locks instead of the global
i_mmap_rwsem. Each VMA is assigned to a shard based on its address
hash (vma_shard_idx), reducing lock contention when multiple CPUs
operate on VMAs mapping the same file.

Key changes:

- __vma_link_file/__remove_shared_vm_struct: Use per-shard tree and
  track vma_count in sharded mode
- vma_prepare/vma_complete: Lock/unlock relevant shard rwsems using
  i_mmap_lock_shards_write/i_mmap_unlock_shards_write
- vma_link_file: Lock per-shard rwsem in sharded mode
- unlink_file_vma_batch_process: Group VMAs by shard, lock shards in
  ascending index order to avoid deadlocks, then remove
- dup_mmap_file_batch:  Collect unique shard locks in sharded mode,
  use vma_interval_tree_insert (not _after) since parent VMA may be
  in a different shard
- i_mmap_lock_shards_write/i_mmap_unlock_shards_write: New helpers
  that collect unique shards from VMA array, sort by index, and
  acquire/release rwsems

Centralized mode behavior is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: GLM <glm@linux.dev>
